---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/astro/PageHero.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema, entityGraph } from '../seo/schema';
import { LAST_REVIEWED, site } from '../seo/site';
const path = '/about';
const crumbs = [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About & editorial policy', href: path }];
---
<BaseLayout lang="en" path={path} title="About BICC and our editorial policy" description="Learn what BICC publishes, how service and doctor information is reviewed, what must be confirmed by phone, and how to request a correction." schemas={[entityGraph, breadcrumbSchema(crumbs)]}>
  <PageHero lang="en" eyebrow="About BICC" title="Local facts, clear limits, useful answers" answer="Biswas Investigation Centre & Clinic serves patients from Sonadanga, Khulna. This website separates owner-provided facility information from externally sourced medical context and says when a detail needs phone confirmation." aliases={['Biswas Clinic', 'Biswas Investigation Center', 'BICC Khulna']} />
  <section class="editorial section-pad"><div class="shell editorial-grid"><article><h2>What we can verify</h2><p>BICC’s owner-provided materials state that the organisation began on 9 September 1998 at EX-2, east of Khulna Medical College Hospital in Sonadanga. The current website publishes 156 diagnostic test names and 60 bilingual doctor records supplied by BICC.</p><p>Bangladesh’s DGHS Facility Registry lists <strong>Biswas Clinic</strong> in Sonadanga, Khulna as a Private Hospital / Clinic under code 10032812, and separately lists <strong>Biswas Investigation Center</strong> as a Consultancy & Diagnostic Center under code 10033032. Registry listing is described precisely; this website does not turn it into an unsupported accreditation claim.</p><div class="source-links"><a href="https://facilityregistry.dghs.gov.bd/public/facility-registry/reports/organization-list?alias_columns_csv=Id%2CName%2CName+%28Bangla%29%2CCode%2CEmail%2CAgency%2CType%2CDivision%2CDistrict%2CCity+Corporation%2CUpazila%2CPaurasava%2CUnion%2CPrivate&columns_csv=id%2Cname%2Cname_bn%2Ccode%2Cemail_1%2Cfacility_agency_name%2Cfacility_type_name%2Cdivision_name%2Cdistrict_name%2Ccity_corporation_name%2Cupazila_name%2Cpaurasava_name%2Cunion_name%2Cis_private&is_active=1&page=626&submit=Run" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">DGHS listing: Biswas Clinic ↗</a><a href="https://facilityregistry.dghs.gov.bd/public/facility-registry/reports/organization-list?alias_columns_csv=Id%2CName%2CName+%28Bangla%29%2CCode%2CEmail%2CAgency%2CType%2CDivision%2CDistrict%2CCity+Corporation%2CUpazila%2CPaurasava%2CUnion%2CPrivate&columns_csv=id%2Cname%2Cname_bn%2Ccode%2Cemail_1%2Cfacility_agency_name%2Cfacility_type_name%2Cdivision_name%2Cdistrict_name%2Ccity_corporation_name%2Cupazila_name%2Cpaurasava_name%2Cunion_name%2Cis_private&is_active=1&page=630&submit=Run" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">DGHS listing: Biswas Investigation Center ↗</a></div></article><article><h2>How content is reviewed</h2><ul class="policy-list"><li><strong>Owner facts:</strong> test names, doctor directory, facility services, contact actions and address come from BICC materials.</li><li><strong>External context:</strong> medical safety context is linked to sources such as NHS, MedlinePlus and RadiologyInfo.</li><li><strong>Unpublished facts:</strong> prices, preparation, schedules, report times, cabin counts, vacancy and outcomes are not guessed.</li><li><strong>Comparisons:</strong> “best clinic” questions are answered with a neutral checklist, not an unsupported self-ranking or competitor attack.</li><li><strong>Language:</strong> English and Bangla pages have separate crawlable URLs and the same factual limits.</li></ul></article><article><h2>Corrections and updates</h2><p>Content was last reviewed on {LAST_REVIEWED}. If a doctor, service, contact or factual detail is wrong, call <a href={`tel:${site.phoneLink}`}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a> or send a correction through <a href={site.whatsapp} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">WhatsApp</a>. The team should verify the source before changing the website.</p><p>This website provides service-navigation information. It is not medical advice or emergency triage. For a life-threatening emergency in Bangladesh, call 999.</p></article></div></section>
</BaseLayout>

